# Data Fetching & Cache Invalidation

TanStack Query is the single client-side cache. Supabase Realtime auto-invalidates via `src/components/RealtimeInvalidationBridge.tsx`.

## For new client-side data fetching

1. Use `useQuery` with a key from `src/lib/query/keys.ts` — add new keys there, never inline ad-hoc keys for shared entities
2. Scope child keys under a registry prefix (e.g. `[...keys.stories, 'with-audio']`) so table-level invalidation covers them
3. After mutations, call `queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: keys.X })` for instant updates (Realtime is the backstop, not the primary path)
4. NEVER use `useEffect` + `useState` fetch-on-mount for shared entity data (older pages that do this predate the pattern — migrate them when touched, don't copy them)
5. NEVER add manual refresh wiring (window events, prop-drilled callbacks) — invalidate the query key instead

## When adding a new core table that client queries depend on

1. Map it in `TABLE_TO_KEYS` in `src/lib/query/keys.ts`
2. Add it to the realtime publication via migration: `ALTER PUBLICATION supabase_realtime ADD TABLE public.<table>`

## Studio contexts

`LifeVisionStudioContext`, `JournalStudioContext`, etc. are query-backed; their `refresh*()` functions invalidate query keys. Keep their public APIs stable.
